; expect-error: E_FFI_RESTRICTED
; expect-at: extern-runtime-entry.zyl:7:1
; A runtime entry's type comes from the compiler's signature table. The
; extern is what is wrong, so the diagnostic points at the extern -- not
; at every ffi-call to the symbol, which located the reader's mistake in
; stdlib/core/show.zyl, a line they never wrote.
(extern "zyl_int_text" (Int) Int)

(defn main () 0)
